Rust 2021, tokio 1.x. Two background tasks can call `rotate_log` at nearly the same time. Every caller goes through `rotate_lock`, yet about once a week the `.1` file contains only a header line and a day of logs is gone. Why?

```rust
pub struct AppState {
    rotate_lock: tokio::sync::Mutex<()>,
    log_path: PathBuf,
}

async fn rotate_log(state: &AppState) -> std::io::Result<()> {
    let _ = state.rotate_lock.lock().await;
    let rotated = state.log_path.with_extension("1");
    tokio::fs::rename(&state.log_path, &rotated).await?;
    let mut f = tokio::fs::File::create(&state.log_path).await?;
    f.write_all(format!("# rotated at {}\n", now_rfc3339()).as_bytes()).await?;
    Ok(())
}
```

